# <binary> <test or *> <mode> <reason>
# binary: a --test target name, lib (library unit tests) or bin-<name> (that binary's unit tests)
# mode: skip (not run under memcheck) | api-errors-no (run alone with --report-api-errors no)
# An api-errors-no test is still memchecked; only driver API error reporting is off, for that test only.
signed_gpu      *                                                      skip           no CUDA call: mock backend and CPU fits; memcheck exits 255 (terminated before first instrumented API call)
gpu_memory_plan a_refused_device_allocation_is_reported_with_its_bytes api-errors-no  provokes a cudaMalloc out-of-memory on purpose
gpu_ring        stale_cuda_error_does_not_fail_the_transport           api-errors-no  provokes a cudaMalloc out-of-memory on purpose
gpu_launch_guard malloc_argument_is_refused_before_the_kernel_runs       api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_launch_guard stack_argument_is_refused                               api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_launch_guard pinned_argument_is_refused                              api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_launch_guard by_value_struct_with_a_host_member_is_refused           api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_launch_guard opt_out_disables_the_check                              api-errors-no  refuses a launch on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_refusal_cli explicit_gpu_run_fails_closed_when_a_launch_is_refused  api-errors-no  forces a launch refusal on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
gpu_refusal_cli auto_dispatch_falls_back_to_the_cpu_with_the_cause_and_the_cpu_archive api-errors-no  forces a launch refusal on purpose; the refusal is a cudaErrorInvalidValue API error
